+      "truth": "The supplied specification instead names ‘Regulation of investigatory powers act 2016’, but the official Act is the Regulation of Investigatory Powers Act 2000; the current UK data-protection framework is UK GDPR plus the Data Protection Act 2018. Either retain the legally accurate names and flag the specification defect, or mirror the supplied specification throughout. Recommend retaining legal accuracy and escalating the specification conflict to the curriculum owner.",
